1
00:06:17,142 --> 00:06:23,142
Freedom. Country. Honor. Passion. To save his best
friend, one man must risk everything he loves.

2
00:12:34,285 --> 00:12:40,285
The Four Feathers is a action, adventure, drama film directed by Shekhar Kapur.

3
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:57,428
A young British officer resigns his post when he learns of his regiment's
plan to ship out to the Sudan for the conflict with the Mahdi.

4
00:25:08,571 --> 00:25:14,571
His friends and fiancée send him four white feathers as
symbols of what they view as his cowardice.

5
00:31:25,714 --> 00:31:31,714
To redeem his honor, he disguises himself as an
Arab and secretly saves their lives.

6
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Harry Faversham, played by Heath Ledger.

7
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Jack Durrance, played by Wes Bentley.

8
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
Ethne Eustace, played by Kate Hudson.

9
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Abou Fatma, played by Djimon Hounsou.

10
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
Colonel Hamilton, played by Alex Jennings.

11
01:09:08,571 --> 01:09:14,571
William Trench, played by Michael Sheen.

12
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The Four Feathers is a 2002 war drama film directed by Shekhar Kapur and
starring Heath Ledger, Wes Bentley, Djimon Hounsou and Kate Hudson.

13
01:21:42,857 --> 01:21:48,857
Set during the British Army's Gordon Relief Expedition (late 1884 to early 1885) in Sudan, well after
the formation of Mahdiyya, it tells the story of a young man accused of cowardice.

14
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
This film, with altered plot events, is the latest in a long line of
cinematic adaptations of the 1902 novel The Four Feathers by A.E.W.

15
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
Other versions of the story have been set in the
1890s, with different battle events.

16
01:40:34,285 --> 01:40:40,285
It was roughly based on the White Feather Campaign during World War I.

17
01:46:51,428 --> 01:46:57,428
The Four Feathers was released on 20 September 2002 by Paramount Pictures in the
United States and by Miramax International in international markets.

18
01:53:08,571 --> 01:53:14,571
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed
$29 million against a $35 million budget.

19
01:59:25,714 --> 01:59:31,714
The film explores themes of army, escape, bravery, loyalty, british empire.

20
02:05:42,857 --> 02:05:48,857
The tone is emotional.
